From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charles Kerr <charles@charleskerr.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:17:16 -0500
Subject: Revert GTK module pinning on Linux

Backports the parts of https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8488311
that apply to M156:

* Reverts "[ui/gtk] Pin gtk-modules to an empty string during
  initialization" (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8243490).
  The pin runs after GTK has loaded the modules listed in settings.ini
  and XSETTINGS, so it unloads them while their callbacks are still
  registered. appmenu-gtk-module, used for KDE Plasma's global menu,
  has a D-Bus name watch pending, so the browser process crashes at
  startup. colorreload-gtk-module and window-decorations-gtk-module,
  which Plasma's GTK integration adds to gtk-modules, watch colors.css
  and the GTK theme name, so the browser process crashes when the
  desktop theme changes. See
  https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/54782 and
  crbug.com/551107198.
* Reverts "[ui/gtk] Sanitize gtk-modules in interceptor and install early"
  (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8296244),
  which also removed GTK_MODULES from the process environment and so from
  child processes.

Upstream's change also removes the GtkSettings interceptor and the CFI
exemption for it. M156 still uses the interceptor to sanitize theme
names, so both are kept here.

This patch can be removed once Electron's Chromium includes 8488311.

diff --git a/ui/gtk/gtk_ui.cc b/ui/gtk/gtk_ui.cc
index ce43b29eb301a846c84f26811b8632d737e91a5f..7333c23ff5529cd40a74f03cfebfaddc97cb9261 100644
--- a/ui/gtk/gtk_ui.cc
+++ b/ui/gtk/gtk_ui.cc
@@ -321,11 +321,6 @@ bool GtkUi::Initialize() {
     return false;
   }
 
-  // The GtkSettings interceptor must be installed early (before GTK
-  // initialization like gtk_init_check()) to intercept and sanitize
-  // settings such as gtk-modules when initial XSETTINGS are read.
-  InstallGtkSettingsInterceptor();
-
   // Gtk initialization through pango may call FcInit() before we get to that.
   // Retrieve global FontConfig config here to call FcInit() with configuration
   // we control.
@@ -337,9 +332,6 @@ bool GtkUi::Initialize() {
   // do it once it is ready.
   std::unique_ptr<base::Environment> env(base::Environment::Create());
   env->SetVar("NO_AT_BRIDGE", "1");
-  // GTK's module loading mechanism can be bypassed with the GTK_MODULES
-  // environment variable, so unset it here.
-  env->UnSetVar("GTK_MODULES");
 
   // When GDK opens the display during gtk_init() it probes it for OpenGL
   // support (GLX/EGL version and extension queries), which loads the GL
@@ -392,16 +384,11 @@ bool GtkUi::Initialize() {
   };
 
   GtkSettings* settings = gtk_settings_get_default();
-  if (!GtkCheckVersion(4)) {
-    // Pin `gtk-modules` to an empty string with APPLICATION source priority
-    // to prevent XSETTINGS updates from loading GTK modules.  GTK4 does not
-    // have this property.
-    g_object_set(settings, "gtk-modules", "", nullptr);
-  }
   SanitizeIconThemeName();
   SanitizeThemeName();
   SanitizeCursorThemeName();
   SanitizeCursorThemeSize();
+  InstallGtkSettingsInterceptor();
 
   if (!GtkCheckVersion(4)) {
     SanitizeKeyThemeName();
diff --git a/ui/gtk/gtk_util.cc b/ui/gtk/gtk_util.cc
